ack-box interaction analysis can surface emergent coordination strategies, offering a scalable complement to internal probe-based interpretability methods.\nL61: Anthology ID:\nL62:     2025.blackboxnlp-1.12\nL63: Volume:\nL64:     cite27†Proceedings of the 8th BlackboxNLP Workshop: Analyzing and Interpreting Neural Networks for NLP L65: Month:\nL66:     November\nL67: Year:\nL68:     2025\nL69: Address:\nL70:     Suzhou, China\nL71: Editors:\nL72:     cite28†Yonatan Belinkov , cite29†Aaron Mueller , cite30†Najoung Kim , cite31†Hosein Mohebbi , cite32†Hanjie Chen , cite33†Dana Arad , cite34†Gabriele Sarti L73: Venues:\nL74:     cite35†BlackboxNLP | cite36†WS L75: SIG:\nL76: \nL77: Publisher:\nL78:     Association for Computational Linguistics\nL79: Note:\nL80: \nL81: Pages:\nL82:     206–225\nL83: Language:\nL84: \nL85: URL:\nL86:     cite37†https://aclanthology.org/2025.blackboxnlp-1.12/ L87: DOI:\nL88:     cite38†10.18653/v1/2025.blackboxnlp-1.12†doi.org L89: Bibkey:\nL90: \nL91: Cite (ACL):\nL92:     Angelina Parfenova, Alexander Denzler, and Jürgen Pfeffer. 2025. cite37†Emergent Convergence in Multi-Agent LLM Annotation . In Proceedings of the 8th BlackboxNLP Workshop: Analyzing and Interpreting Neural Networks for NLP, pages 206–225, Suzhou, China. Association for Computational Linguistics.\nL93: Cite (Informal):\nL94:     cite37†Emergent Convergence in Multi-Agent LLM Annotation (Parfenova et al., BlackboxNLP 2025)\nL95: Copy Citation:\nL96:     [Button: More options…]\nL97: PDF:\nL98:     cite23†https://aclanthology.org/2025.blackboxnlp-1.12.pdf L99: cite23†PDF cite0†Cite cite0†Fix data L100: \nL101: * * *\nL102: ##### Export citation\nL103: \nL104:     @inproceedings{parfenova-etal-2025-emergent,\nL105:         title = \"Emergent Convergence in Multi-Agent {LLM} Annotation\",\nL106:         author = {Parfenova, Angelina  and\nL107:           Denzler, Alexander  and\nL108:           Pfeffer, J{\\\"u}rgen},